WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.600
Bored...

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.210
Anything interesting to talk about?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.170
Um...

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.420
I read a book a while ago.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.700
What was it called?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.740
Well, I forgot the title.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.290
Tell me what kind of story it was.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.490
Yes.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.360
It was the tale of a man in love with scientific technology.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.420
A robot birthed by the pinnacle of science-

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.430
Tetsujin 28-0!

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.610
One who plotted to use a robot birthed by the pinnacle of science-

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.330
Giant Hobo!

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.430
A genius scientist, planning to use a robot birthed by the pinnacle of science-

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.330
Maybe-ginger Z!

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.330
as a replacement for his lost son,

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.600
created an advanced artificial human possessing

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.440
weapons, amazing physical abilities, and emotions.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.150
But this robot's body did not grow as a human's does.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.030
Astro Roy!

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:07.290
The robot, built by the scientist's grandson from plans he'd left behind,

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.190
had a phrase he would always say.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.180
<i>By George, I've got it!</i>

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.150
Let's go back, Kanako.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.340
I did what I had to.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.280
Yayoi...

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.760
There was a purpose to these bodies of ours. A very important one.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.710
Now that I've done what I had to,
I've never been so happy.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.340
So I'm fine.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.040
No matter what happens to us, I'm fine.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.630
I see. Yes, I understand.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.620
We're going back.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.890
Yes.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:32.650
No matter how many years pass,
the warmth of summer never changes.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:40.820
So, whenever this season comes around,
I remember the summer of my thirteenth year,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.300
my days as a young boy, when I knew nothing at all.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:49.960
Even now, it remains unchanged within me.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.610
She really will get better, right?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:59.960
We ethereal spirits require a special energy, which you might call "existence."

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.340
Existence?

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:08.680
Yayoi and I have maintained ourselves this long by exchanging our little remaining power.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.390
If I return the power of existence that I took from her...

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.060
Arashi-san...

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.020
Where am I?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.900
How did I...

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.630
Everybody...

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.120
Arashi-san!

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.590
Hajime-chan?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.180
I'm so glad... I'm so glad you're back...

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.170
Come on... What's wrong, Hajime-chan?

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.170
You're safe now.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.930
Fushimi-san? Yamazaki-san?

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.560
Everyone, sorry for the trouble we caused.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.820
Our desire to protect ourselves ended up hurting you.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.900
So we must accept the punishment for that.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.470
No way.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:14.880
Just now, we used almost all the power of existence we had.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.170
Don't worry.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.910
We've made our peace.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.360
Right, Yayoi?

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:20.970
Right.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.210
No! Wait!

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.230
Thank you for everything, Hajime-chan.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.120
Wait!

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.730
Goodbye.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.200
Both of you, don't do this!

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.390
Hajime-chan!

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.270
Jun!

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.460
Our existence returned.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.450
Why?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.450
You see,

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.650
I have Hajime-chan, a person I connected with.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:03.750
When we connect with someone in this era,
it seems that our wavering existence comes back.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:04.470
What?

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.290
I don't know if it's from forcing us to consider existence,

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.250
or if, perhaps, we touch the power of life.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:13.170
Then if we...

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.440
If you find someone you can connect with,

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.180
you won't disappear.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.360
Let Your Body Ride on the Flow of Time
Master

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.990
Jeez, what a mess.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:31.450
If you weren't hiding in a mansion, but went out and met people, you would've learned this...

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:36.210
You can't do anything careless while trying to protect a girl in a wheelchair.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.910
It's all good. Everything worked out.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:45.430
I see. Yayoi-chan and Yamazaki-san,
you both became ethereal spirits that day.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.480
Yes, the next thing I knew, I was like this.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:53.070
I had no idea there were others like Arashi and myself.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.840
What happened to us is sad,
but I'm happy we met again.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.060
Yes.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.900
I'm truly happy to meet you and Arashi-san again!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.910
Let's work together going forward.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:07.740
But, we need to find you two a partner to connect with.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:12.910
Don't worry. For now, he's going to give us energy.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.100
Huh? Hey, the hell I will-

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.280
You don't have any other work, right?

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.560
I'll hire you for this and for work at the mansion-

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.610
No way!

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.200
I'm not working with you...

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.120
What?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.660
Didn't you want to become a courageous person,
who would risk their life to save someone?

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.930
Like Arashi-san?

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.920
How the hell did you...

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.890
Is the Arashi who saved my dad's life...

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.340
You wouldn't abandon an old friend of hers, would you?

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.820
OK, that's settled.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:45.610
Wait!

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.350
Not yet.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:55.370
We've caused trouble for you all, and we owe you for helping us.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:58.150
We must apologize and also pay you back.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:00.970
Don't worry about it.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.480
That's not good enough.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.820
Anything-name it!

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.670
Then how about this?

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:13.950
Um, this is...

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.830
Paying us back.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.350
You're going to be a waitress here.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.700
No way!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.570
Why do we have to-

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.770
You said "anything."

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.100
That's pretty cute, Kanako!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.540
You actually look kind of hot, Kanako!

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.990
It's cute, Yamazaki-san!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.550
This is great!

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:39.370
I guess if she puts on cute clothes, she actually looks like a woman.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:44.440
Well, you know what they say, the clothes make the woman!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:51.020
Seriously, that spooky woman being a nice, cheerful waitress...

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.960
What the hell was that for?!

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.380
Make fun of my girls, and you pay.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:02.220
I think that's going too far, though!

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:06.770
I am Fushimi Yayoi.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.270
Nice to meet you all.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.330
A new girl?

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.790
You're pretty.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:16.200
I love how this place has so many kind, gentle girls.
You don't see it much anymore, Sensei!

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.910
Exactly what I was after.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:20.770
Welcome!

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:26.610
Youko?

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.760
My shoot was nearby, so I came in to say "hi."

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.830
W-Wait... The fact that I'm a model is a secret here.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.350
Don't worry. I know.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.000
Hello.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.170
I'm Himekawa Youko,

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.880
Kamigamo Jun's girlfriend.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:49.580
Silly Jun won't tell me anything about his job.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:54.100
I was lonely, so I came to see what it's like.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.510
Think of this as practice.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.240
It's your chance to be a total guy.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.460
Salt, please.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.160
<i>Unforgivable!</i>

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.480
You're cheating on Kaya-san?

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.780
Um, well...

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.130
Only you know that I'm a girl.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.980
Trick him somehow!

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.290
How awful!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:20.920
Jun has been engaging in trysts with a young lass, despite already having me!

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.710
I believed in you.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:26.960
But I knew nothing... Nothing, as you toyed with my pure emotions!

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.830
That's not what I meant!

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.060
Give me the salt.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:34.670
How terrible! You were being a cheat?

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:36.560
Youko!

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.600
I hate you!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.700
I'm going to kill you, and then die myself!

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.690
Salt, I said. Salt!

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.390
A man should never make a girl cry!

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.530
I'm going to beat the crap out of you!

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.990
Don't believe them, idiot!

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:51.860
And Youko, stop interfering with my job and go home!

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.820
What? I'm a customer. What's wrong with that?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.380
They seem to be fighting over something.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.800
Fools in love...

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.000
Ignore them.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.160
But they helped us. And as friends, we can't just ignore them.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.150
Yayoi!

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.410
Um...

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.350
Yes?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.650
I'm sorry to interrupt,

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:16.600
but I think you should be more openhearted and calm in your dealings with gentlemen.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.700
Huh?

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.120
Especially when you deal with a lover,

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:25.240
fighting and worsening things will prevent you from reaching an acceptable solution.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.820
Please contain your anger.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.830
You're wrong.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:37.820
If you repress anger just 'cause you're a girl, unhappiness will build, wrecking the relationship.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:42.060
And love is more fun when you can express yourself!

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.030
What?!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:46.100
Keeping quiet only means you'll cry later.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:51.020
And bitching him out is the only way to make the guy improve.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.360
Anyway, iced coffee.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.270
And salt for me, too.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.690
OK!

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:01.230
Here you are.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.520
S-Salt...

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.400
Kanako, calm down!

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.570
You don't need to suck up to a brat like this!

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.020
But she's a customer.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:15.120
Girls who don't consider those around them make me angry.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.980
You're the one not considering people around them!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:23.280
Jeez... Yayoi-san's OK,
but Kanako's one violent woman.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.820
She's lived through some tough times.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:28.200
Arashi-san...

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:32.560
But meeting old acquaintances makes me remember the past.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:37.490
Sometimes, you act like an old woman.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.320
Cold!

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.160
I'm sorry, Hajime-chan.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:44.960
I just thought, sometimes,
you act younger than you are.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.500
I guess it really bugs you, huh?

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.140
That's cold!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.110
Watch where you're throwing that!

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:52.690
Cold!

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:55.660
My, you're certainly energetic.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:56.870
I'm sorry.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:59.620
Come inside! I'll dry you off!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.690
My, you're...

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:04.880
It's good to see you again.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.950
<i>Dreams open up the night...</i>

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.820
I'm really sorry.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.470
I'll dry it right away.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.830
Don't worry about it so much.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.270
I'm done with work for the day.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:25.470
You're really careless. This happened because you were messing around.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.170
Kaya-san, do you know that guy?

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.750
It looks like he knows Arashi-san.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.070
I thought that maybe he was another ghost from the same era...

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.720
No, I don't remember him.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.130
I see.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.770
Which means he's from our time?

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.730
Um, so...

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.650
You know me?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.440
I'm sorry.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.920
I must have startled you earlier.

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:50.290
I've met you before.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.890
Met me?

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.900
I'm Yamashiro Takeshi.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:55.690
Do you remember that name?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.820
Yamashiro Takeshi?

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.320
Fool.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:01.600
Rush yourself, and you lose the real target.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:04.360
Hey, that's kind of nice.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.770
Even if she was born long ago, she's got a 16-year-old's body.

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:10.000
That's the time for love...

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.010
Arashiyama-sempai

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:13.280
in love?

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.830
That's kind of rare to see.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.560
Just talking about love is embarrassing?

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.260
She's coming back.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.610
So, whaddya think?

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.980
Seems like you were having a nice chat.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:30.450
He says he knows me.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:35.610
That's Arashiyama-sempai! She was
famously popular, even at the girl's school.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:38.050
But I don't remember him.

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:40.460
You don't think it's an excuse to pick you up?

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.950
My, how shameless.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:44.710
Such friendly talk with a guy you don't know.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.400
So, what are you going to do?

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.300
Well, you see...

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.220
He invited me on a date.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:55.550
A-And did you accept?

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:57.960
I had no reason to refuse.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:14:59.810
Shameless hussy!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.580
Yayoi, don't listen anymore!

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.080
Are you sure it's OK to meet people from this era carelessly?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:09.070
If people find out who we are, it'll be bad.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.320
But, um, how to put it?

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.170
I can't ignore him.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.470
Well, Hajime-chan?

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:21.310
I'm pretty cute, huh?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.620
You can't say I look old now, can you?

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.680
Hmph, it doesn't help at all.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.980
Where are you going?

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.540
To clean the toilets.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:38.360
You're going in that kimono?

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.540
I would've given you what I wear for dates.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.190
What you wear for dates?

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:44.020
Something really sexy...

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.300
Including underwear.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.840
I think this is probably for the best.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.830
You set, Arashi-san?

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.030
Yes! Let's go.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:56.810
I'm worried.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.640
How wonderful, Arashiyama-sempai!

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.650
A beautiful love that bridges time...

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:02.720
I'm so envious.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.420
Slattern!

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.050
Yayoi, don't end up like that.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.370
Where's Hajime-chan?

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.070
He said he was going shopping.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:12.820
On his bike?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.210
Yeah, a bike...

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.480
This is the first day I can enjoy the local sights in a long time.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.900
Anywhere you want to go?

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:27.200
Do you remember the place where we met?

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.830
Yes, of course.

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:30.920
Then let's go there, if that's all right.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:35.260
That's fine. I wanted to take you there myself.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:44.230
What am I trying to do here?

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.890
It doesn't matter.

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:47.110
This is between men!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.690
And I ain't losing this fight, asshole!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.320
I'll do whatever it takes!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.230
This is where you met me?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:13.100
I went into the night sea here.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.250
No way.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:15.700
Something pushed you too far, and...

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.630
No, just too many people here during the day.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:25.480
Stuff was bothering me,
and I decided I wanted a swim.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.390
So I went into the sea, clothes still on.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:31.490
But the waves were stronger than I'd thought.

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:35.490
I realized the danger and tried to turn back,
but the waves pulled me further and further out.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.610
I tried calling for help, but no one was there.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.750
The black sea was the only thing around me.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.940
The cold waves sapped my strength.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.590
I thought I was a goner.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:49.860
But then she saved me.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:57.580
I don't remember how, but the next thing I knew, I was being lectured back on the beach.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:00.610
She looked exactly like you.

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:03.140
This girl, ten years ago...

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:09.990
I know, ten years ago, it wasn't you.

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.560
But you looked so much like her,
I had to say something.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.610
I see.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:16.400
I'm sorry.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.910
No.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.490
It was an interesting story.

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:24.290
I'm back.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.530
Welcome back, Arashiyama-sempai!

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:28.920
So, how'd it go?

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.530
It was fun!

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:34.810
We went for a drive, and then to the sea,
and we ate, and he brought me back.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.310
Nice, sempai! You're really getting far!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.840
Foul strumpet...

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.920
Yayoi, make sure you don't do that.

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.970
Is that all?

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.520
He didn't do anything weird?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.300
No, he was a good guy.

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:52.330
That's why I said I'd lend you my date clothes.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.410
What happened to you, Hajime-chan?

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.670
Those wounds...

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:59.520
Hajime has thrown off the woman of his past and been reborn.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:00.820
Shut up!

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:01.610
Don't talk to me!

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:04.970
Don't cry. Half the world's population is female-

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.460
I'm not crying. And I don't care.

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.740
A man's gotta know when to give up.

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:11.300
He seems like a nice guy, huh?

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:15.290
I'll give up, but I'll still help you go through time.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:19.010
I don't leave things halfway done.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.500
Don't worry about it.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.240
Hey, Hajime-chan.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:27.770
I found out something when I was with him.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:33.360
I had never met him.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:39.230
But in his past, I saved him.

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:41.000
So I figured it out...

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.690
He's somebody I saved in the future.

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:50.590
I wanted to find out more,

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:54.970
but the only way would be spending time with him directly and feeling it out.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:58.200
Oh, so that's why you went on a date with him?

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:00.600
Boring.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.880
Sorry to worry you, Hajime-chan.

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:07.170
I knew it the whole time!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.330
I believed in you, Arashi-san!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.340
Idiot.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.210
I want to save him.

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:16.070
Will you go with me, Hajime-chan?

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:18.140
If you insist!

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:24.130
Bastard's causing trouble for us.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.550
Let's go, Arashi-san!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:26.750
Yeah!

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:34.540
That was quite the commotion.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:38.040
Yeah, but it all ended well.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.230
I'm glad he's safe.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.610
Yamashiro-san and us, too...

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.930
When we're all together, it's like we've gone back to that time.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.680
It's just as it was in the past.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:53.680
Yes. It's like this place alone has gone back in time.

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:58.690
Yeah, but it was Hajime-chan who brought us all together.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.190
Arashi-san!

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:05.400
The master says she's having a welcome party!

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:08.270
Wow, that's nice of her.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:11.760
She just wants a reason to drink and party.

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:13.800
That sounds like her.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:17.410
It's possible that a boy can grow up in a single summer...

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:20.710
Arashi-san, hurry!

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:23.830
It's cute how he's the only one who doesn't know.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:26.180
Yeah, I'm coming!

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:25.190
How are you, Yayoi?

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:27.930
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:30.290
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:33.640
I read another fascinating book.

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:36.440
My, what was it called?

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:41.120
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:43.530
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:45.620
Yes, gladly.

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:51.040
It was a story that crossed time.

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:56.640
It was the story of a girl who meets a boy,
after sixty years have passed.

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:00.970
The girl invites the boy on a dramatic adventure...

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:04.420
My, what a wonderful, heartwarming story.

00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:08.070
The narrator in this story had a phrase he would always say.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:10.290
What was it? Tell me.

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:16.450
No matter how many years pass,
the warmth of summer never changes.

00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:21.850
So, whenever this season comes around,
I remember the summer of my thirteenth year,

00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:24.720
my days as a young boy, when I knew nothing at all.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:29.750
Even now, it remains unchanged within me.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.390
When you think of summer-

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:33.870
You think of snow cones!

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:37.180
Eat them too fast and you'll get a brain freeze.

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:38.680
That goes away if you drink water.

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:41.760
Fin

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:40.520
Old women know lots of stuff!

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:41.380
The hell you say?

00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:44.040
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:50.150
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:50.150
Illustration by Mako Aboshi
